  "description": "Porch, living room, dining room and kitchen in a line, with bedrooms off a short hall to one side. The first mass-market American plan to abandon the formal parlor: the living and dining rooms flow together around a hearth and the front door opens straight into the life of the house. It deliberately does not carry an entry sequence: porch, then living room, one threshold, and the informality is an argument rather than an omission.",
